  "date": "2014-09",
  "title": "Flight Of Discovery Over Switzerland",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "Switzerland's transformation from intact agricultural land with scattered factories to the heavily built-up country it is today is particularly striking from the air.\n\nThe holding curated by ETH-Bibliothek's Image Archive contains around 135,000 aerial photographs spanning almost a century, from which 150 impressive oblique and vertical views were selected for the book from the \"Pictorial Worlds\" series.\n\nYou can browse through a selection of the photographs on the Bildarchiv Online platform.\n\nWe have also compiled some additional information and photos on the ETHeritage blog.\n\nThe book can be purchased from ETH-Bibliothek's Collections and Archives reading room or book shops."
    }
  ],
